## Source integration — bounded management-fragment RX

`ManagementReassembly.{hpp,cpp}` now runs as a fixed-capacity RX stage in
`WifiEngine::acceptRx` after the caller attests DMA/FCS and channel policy.
It publishes no management payload before contiguous fragments match the
original subtype, sequence number and all three 802.11 addresses. The owner
rejects out-of-order, stale (>500-ms), clock-regressed, overlength and PMF-
protected fragments, and clears pending state on scan replacement, new join,
rejection, radio stop and an invalid RX trust lease. Completed frames are
borrowed only during the synchronous scan/association/link handler. The
standalone `parseFrame` still refuses raw management fragments.

This is a source-only reassembly path included in the normal Xcode target;
it does not authenticate non-PMF management frames, establish physical FCS,
wire RF or prove scan operation. PMF reassembly and negotiation, independent
receive-channel calibration, aggregation, BlockAck and native response timing
remain outstanding. The P2 task stays open pending those integrations.

## Source integration — bounded open-data fragment RX

`DataReassembly.{hpp,cpp}` now joins `WifiEngine::acceptRx` after verified
DMA/FCS and before the existing station address, LLC/SNAP and replay/duplicate
admission. It retains only one ordered, matching unprotected FromDS data/QoS
fragment stream, bounded by a 2342-byte reconstructed MPDU and 500-ms
monotonic deadline. Partial payloads cannot escape. Assembly is reset on
association, scan, radio and trust changes; success consumes one complete
802.11 sequence number at the existing native-payload gate. C++14/C++17
synthetic regressions cover order, identity, QoS, time, overflow, aliasing,
trust revocation and actual open-association delivery.

Each fragment still requires external verified DMA/FCS evidence, which portable
tests cannot supply. WPA2 CCMP fragmentation remains explicitly rejected
until independently authenticated per-fragment PN/MIC and controlled RX
lifetime are implemented. This does not complete BlockAck/A-MPDU reordering,
native Ethernet delivery or physical radio permission; keep the task open.
